[{"id":"IU_15","ref":"15","section":"The eighteen mantras","sa":["हिरण्मयेन पात्रेण सत्यस्यापिहितं मुखम् ।","तत् त्वं पूषन्नपावृणु सत्यधर्माय दृष्टये ॥१५॥"],"iast":["hiraṇmayena pātreṇa satyasyāpihitaṃ mukham ।","tat tvaṃ pūṣannapāvṛṇu satyadharmāya dṛṣṭaye ॥15॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The face of Truth is covered with a brilliant golden lid; that do thou remove, O Fosterer, for the law of the Truth, for sight.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 17, p. 9","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["हिरण्मयेन","hiraṇmayena","with a brilliant golden","hiraṇmaya"],["पात्रेण","pātreṇa","lid","pātra"],["सत्यस्य","satyasya","of Truth","satya"],["आपिहितम्","āpihitam","is covered","pidhā"],["मुखम्","mukham","face","mukha"],["तत्","tat","that","tat"],["त्वम्","tvam","thou","tva"],["पूषन्","pūṣan","O Fosterer","pūṣan"],["अपावृणु","apāvṛṇu","do remove","√vṛ"],["सत्य","satya","of the Truth","satya"],["धर्माय","dharmāya","for the law","dharma"],["दृष्टये","dṛṣṭaye","for sight","dṛṣṭi"]],"tr":{"text":"The face of the Truth (ie., Purusha in the solar orb) is veiled by a bright vessel. Mayst thou unveil it, O Sun, so as to be perceived by me whose dharma is truth.","by":"Vidyavachaspati V. Panoli","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/Isopanisad/1.15.mp3","whole":[239.44,253.95]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":16,"up":"isha","takeaway":"The truth is often hidden behind something golden and attractive. Ask for the cover to be removed."}]